==Battleground==
*1 [[Gato Amigo (Enemy)|Gato Amigo]] (200%) spawns after 0.67 seconds<sup>20f</sup>.
*7 [[Gato Amigo (Enemy)|Gato Amigos]] (200%) spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 18~22 seconds<sup>540f~660f</sup>.
*7 [[Gato Amigo (Enemy)|Gato Amigos]] (200%) spawn after 24 seconds<sup>720f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*5 [[Gato Amigo (Enemy)|Gato Amigos]] (200%) spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 23.33~33.33 seconds<sup>700f~1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Gato Amigo (Enemy)|Gato Amigo]] (10%) spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Gato Amigo (Enemy)|Gato Amigos]] (300%) spawn, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
**10 [[Gato Amigo (Enemy)|Gato Amigos]] (300%) spawn, delay 4~12 seconds<sup>120f~360f</sup>.
**10 [[Gato Amigo (Enemy)|Gato Amigos]] (300%) spawn, delay 18~28 seconds<sup>540f~840f</sup>.
**10 [[Gato Amigo (Enemy)|Gato Amigos]] (300%) spawn, delay 21.33~30 seconds<sup>640f~900f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Gato Amigo (Enemy)|Gato Amigos]] (300%) spawn, delay 8~16 seconds<sup>240f~480f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Angelic Sleipnir]]s spawn, delay 120~123.33 seconds<sup>3,600f~3,700f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Bore]]s spawn, delay 53.33~56.67 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Having [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] will be enough to clear out the waves of Gato Amigos in this stage. To kill the Bore, anti-Red crowd-control units such as [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] or [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Enchantress Cat]] are recommended, however not entirely necessary if you have enough damage.

The Angelic Sleipnir will be quite difficult to reach, but they spawn with a two minute delay. Tankier units are recommended to reach and kill them, like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]]. Having Awakened Bahamut Cat makes quick work of Sleipnir through Bahamut chaining, however that requires clearing ItF 3.

==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 9.10 Update|Version 9.10]], there used to be a mistake inside the stage on the top-left corner. The stage name was labeled as "[[Oh Yokozuna! (Insane)]]", which is the name for the second stage of [[Sumo Awakens!]].

